    "enrich_notes": "Vancouver Section 4 (2025) supplements SWMMWW; WQv depth, media depths, ED drawdown, and most BMP sizing criteria are by reference to Ecology Stormwater Manual Vol. III/V. Local numeric highlights: infiltration base minimum 5 ft (60 in) to seasonal high water with possible 3 ft reduction per mounding analysis; maximum allowed design infiltration rate 250 in/hr with Table D-3 correction factors (base CF 2); bioretention may use assumed 12 in/hr for qualifying BSM in WWHM2012/MGS Flood; max ponding 1 ft (12 in); marginal site infiltration threshold <2 in/hr triggers PE design for small-project downspout systems.",
